3. Calculate response-time percentiles and peak throughput
After the test, add these listeners:
- Aggregate Report
- Summary Report
- View Results Tree for debugging only
- A time-series throughput graph, such as jp@gc – Transactions per Second, if installed through Plugins Manager
Run the test, then locate the row for POST /api/order in Aggregate Report.
Metric	Where to find it	What it means
Average response time	Aggregate Report → Average	Mean response time in milliseconds
90th percentile	Aggregate Report → 90% Line	90% of requests completed within this time
95th percentile	Aggregate Report → 95% Line	95% of requests completed within this time
Error percentage	Aggregate Report → Error %	Percentage of failed requests
Peak throughput	Throughput-over-time graph	Highest observed request rate during the test
